WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.915 --> 00:00:21.719
is the time," Ally thought as she and Mateo walked to the park to meet Kate and Bethany.

2
00:00:21.739 --> 00:00:26.163
"As soon as I see Kate, I'm going to tell her the truth about my phone."

3
00:00:28.105 --> 00:00:33.284
But when they found the girls, Kate was so excited about her T-shirt design, Ally didn't want to

4
00:00:33.324 --> 00:00:33.864
interrupt her.

5
00:00:33.884 --> 00:00:38.326
"See?" Kate held out her tablet.

6
00:00:38.346 --> 00:00:44.467
"It's a soccer ball that's been kicked high up into the atmosphere and is circling the sun—like a

7
00:00:44.507 --> 00:00:47.868
planet." "Isn't it stellar?"

8
00:00:48.268 --> 00:00:48.989
Bethany asked.

9
00:00:49.009 --> 00:00:51.869
"It's amazing," Ally said.

10
00:00:51.889 --> 00:00:57.031
"Can we add the words Sandville Soccer Club on the back of the shirts?"

11
00:00:57.491 --> 00:00:58.271
Mateo asked.

12
00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:00.692
"Sure," Kate said.

13
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.021
"And I'll make the letter o in Soccer Club look like a soccer ball."

14
00:01:05.041 --> 00:01:07.502
"Can you send the design to me?

15
00:01:07.882 --> 00:01:10.283
I'll send it to the print shop," Mateo said.

16
00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:15.644
"Sure." Kate made some quick changes to the design and sent it to Mateo.

17
00:01:20.945 --> 00:01:23.386
T-shirts are going to sell like hotcakes!"

18
00:01:23.866 --> 00:01:26.587
Mateo said as he forwarded the design to Eli.

19
00:01:26.967 --> 00:01:27.607
Ally frowned.

20
00:01:27.627 --> 00:01:29.728
"I hope they sell better than that!

21
00:01:30.488 --> 00:01:33.531
Pancakes are not one of the diner's top sellers."

22
00:01:34.091 --> 00:01:36.093
Mateo, Bethany, and Kate laughed.

23
00:01:36.113 --> 00:01:39.235
"You're so funny, Ally!"

24
00:01:39.535 --> 00:01:40.056
Kate said.

25
00:01:40.076 --> 00:01:42.738
"I have the best surprise for you.

26
00:01:42.758 --> 00:01:45.600
I bet you'll never guess what happened."

27
00:01:46.461 --> 00:01:47.242
Bethany grinned.

28
00:01:47.262 --> 00:01:49.583
"You'll never guess!"

29
00:01:50.784 --> 00:01:51.505
"What happened?"

30
00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:52.406
Ally asked.

31
00:01:52.426 --> 00:01:55.508
"No, you have to guess," Kate said.

32
00:01:55.528 --> 00:01:58.571
"I thought you said I'd never guess."

33
00:01:59.051 --> 00:02:00.112
Ally was confused.

34
00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.882
"Never is a very long time.

35
00:02:03.342 --> 00:02:05.964
It's almost as infinite as the universe."

36
00:02:06.705 --> 00:02:09.027
It was Kate and Bethany's turn to be confused.

37
00:02:09.047 --> 00:02:13.670
"Maybe you should just tell us, Kate," Mateo said quickly.

38
00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:16.793
"I found your phone!"

39
00:02:17.093 --> 00:02:17.674
Kate cried.

40
00:02:17.694 --> 00:02:19.715
"You did?"

41
00:02:20.376 --> 00:02:23.158
Ally blinked in surprise and touched her back pocket.

42
00:02:23.639 --> 00:02:25.240
Alpha was safely tucked away there.

43
00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.422
And luckily, she was staying quiet.

44
00:02:27.442 --> 00:02:31.100
"Tell her how it happened, Kate," Bethany said.

45
00:02:32.061 --> 00:02:35.763
Kate pulled an old phone that looked exactly like Alpha from her bag.

46
00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.126
was putting up signs near the diner.

47
00:02:41.626 --> 00:02:44.728
When I looked down, I spotted the phone just lying on the ground.

48
00:02:46.489 --> 00:02:48.450
It must have fallen out of your pocket one day.

49
00:02:48.991 --> 00:02:51.772
If it wasn't so old, someone else would have picked it up.

50
00:02:52.993 --> 00:02:53.713
Here you go!"

51
00:02:53.733 --> 00:02:56.955
"Gosh, thanks so much."

52
00:02:57.695 --> 00:02:58.416
Ally flushed.

53
00:02:58.892 --> 00:03:00.653
How could she explain her fib now?

54
00:03:00.673 --> 00:03:02.734
"Power it up.

55
00:03:03.234 --> 00:03:05.775
Make sure it still works," Bethany said.

56
00:03:05.795 --> 00:03:07.756
"I hope it does.

57
00:03:07.776 --> 00:03:09.957
I love the funny things it says!"

58
00:03:10.397 --> 00:03:11.057
Kate grinned.

59
00:03:12.538 --> 00:03:14.599
Ally gulped and pressed the Power button.

60
00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:17.620
The device lit up instantly.

61
00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:20.321
"What do you think it will say first?"

62
00:03:20.681 --> 00:03:21.782
Kate asked eagerly.

63
00:03:21.802 --> 00:03:26.604
"Um er Ally fumbled for words.

64
00:03:27.148 --> 00:03:30.050
"I don't think this phone is working—" "Of course I'm working!"

65
00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:31.350
Alpha blurted out.

66
00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:35.713
"Wow!" Kate laughed.

67
00:03:36.413 --> 00:03:38.314
"That app is amazing.

68
00:03:38.895 --> 00:03:41.596
The voice sounds like it's coming from your back pocket."

69
00:03:41.616 --> 00:03:44.077
"Ha-ha! Really?"

70
00:03:44.698 --> 00:03:48.140
Ally reached around to her back pocket to try to turn Alpha off.

71
00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:51.582
But as Ally pulled her out, Alpha fell to the ground.

72
00:03:51.602 --> 00:03:53.383
"Oh no!"

73
00:03:53.843 --> 00:03:55.744
Ally thought, looking down in horror.

74
00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:00.967
"Wait, you have your phone?"

75
00:04:01.387 --> 00:04:01.988
Kate frowned.

76
00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:09.654
"I, uh, didn't want to tell you, but I, well, I bought another phone."

77
00:04:10.134 --> 00:04:13.918
As soon as the words came out of her mouth, Ally wanted to take them back.

78
00:04:14.778 --> 00:04:16.460
She had just told another fib!

79
00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.321
"You did?"

80
00:04:18.642 --> 00:04:19.222
Kate asked.

81
00:04:19.242 --> 00:04:23.406
"Why? I told you I'd help you find your old phone."

82
00:04:24.126 --> 00:04:25.868
"I know," Ally said in a rush.

83
00:04:26.348 --> 00:04:27.649
"But I didn't want to bother you.

84
00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:30.792
And besides, the old one isn't working so well."

85
00:04:30.812 --> 00:04:32.533
"I'm working just fine!"

86
00:04:32.914 --> 00:04:33.594
Alpha snapped.

87
00:04:33.614 --> 00:04:35.536
"I can't believe you replaced me!"

88
00:04:36.977 --> 00:04:38.959
Kate and Bethany cracked up, laughing.

89
00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.781
But Ally wanted to cry.

90
00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:44.404
"This is awful," she thought.

91
00:04:44.424 --> 00:04:47.847
"My little fibs are spiraling out of control!"

92
00:04:47.867 --> 00:04:51.130
"Oh, look at the time!"

93
00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:53.732
Mateo said, quickly checking his phone.

94
00:04:54.208 --> 00:04:56.649
"Ally and I have to get home to help my dad with something.

95
00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:58.671
Thanks again for the design, Kate!"

96
00:05:01.752 --> 00:05:03.733
As they hurried away, Ally looked at him.

97
00:05:03.753 --> 00:05:06.335
"What do we need to help Ray with?"

98
00:05:06.355 --> 00:05:08.676
"Nothing," Mateo said.

99
00:05:08.696 --> 00:05:13.359
"I just said that as an excuse to get away before things got worse."

100
00:05:14.359 --> 00:05:14.959
Ally blinked.

101
00:05:14.979 --> 00:05:18.441
"You mean, you told a fib?"

102
00:05:18.461 --> 00:05:20.142
"I guess."

103
00:05:20.603 --> 00:05:21.323
Mateo shrugged.

104
00:05:21.343 --> 00:05:24.249
"It was harmless, and you needed help.

105
00:05:24.989 --> 00:05:27.071
No one was going to get hurt because I said it."

106
00:05:27.771 --> 00:05:28.652
Ally shook her head.

107
00:05:28.672 --> 00:05:33.716
"So, on Earth it's okay to tell a fib if it doesn't hurt anyone?"

108
00:05:33.736 --> 00:05:35.997
"Yep," Mateo said.

109
00:05:36.017 --> 00:05:39.900
"Phew!" Relief washed over Ally.

110
00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.202
"That's great news!"

111
00:05:42.782 --> 00:05:44.824
Now she didn't have to tell Kate the truth!
